1. Core & User Management Modules
👨‍💼 1. User (Base Class)
Purpose: Represents generic user account entity and authentication routines.

Attributes (Fields):
int userId — Unique user identifier
String name — Full name of the user
String email — Registered email/username
String password — Login password credential
String phone — Contact phone number
String role — User system role (Patient, Doctor, Admin)
Methods:
login(): void — Authenticates user credentials against the database
logout(): void — Ends active session and updates logout timestamp
updateProfile(): void — Edits user account details (name, phone, etc.)
changePassword(): void — Changes and updates current password
downloadPatientHistory(): void — Exports complete patient medical summary to text file
🩺 2. Patient (Extends User)
Purpose: Manages patient-specific profiles, appointment bookings, queue tracking, and personal medical records.

Attributes (Fields):
int patientId — Unique patient ID
String gender — Patient gender
int age — Patient age in years
String bloodGroup — Blood group
String address — Residential address
String healthId — Unique Health ID badge (HCXXXXX)
Methods:
loadPatientDetails(): void — Fetches profile information from database
getPatientId(): int — Returns current patient ID
bookAppointment(): void — Schedules appointment with a specific doctor
viewMedicalHistory(): void — Displays past medical history entries
viewPrescription(): void — Displays prescribed medications and instructions
viewDietPlan(): void — Views active custom diet plan
viewReports(): void — Displays generated lab test reports
viewDashboard(): void — Displays patient dashboard metrics
displayQueueStatus(): void — Checks live doctor queue position & estimated waiting time (peopleAhead * 15 mins)
👨‍⚕️ 3. Doctor (Extends User)
Purpose: Handles doctor profile management, appointment views, patient treatments, prescriptions, and diet plans.

Attributes (Fields):
String specialization — Medical domain/specialty
int experience — Years of clinical experience
boolean available — Availability status (true/false)
Methods:
loadDoctorDetails(): void — Loads doctor details and consultation hours
getDoctorId(): int — Returns current doctor ID
viewAppointments(): void — Displays scheduled appointments categorized into Today, Upcoming, and Past
createReport(): void — Diagnoses patient and creates medical report
createPrescription(): void — Prescribes medicines and dosage instructions
createDietPlan(): void — Formulates disease-specific diet plans for patients
showFollowUpsAndReply(): void — Reviews patient follow-up queries and submits doctor replies
showNextAppointment(): void — Displays the next token/appointment in queue
viewLiveQueue(): void — Views doctor’s active waiting queue sorted by priority
viewDashboard(): void — Displays doctor dashboard analytics
⚙️ 4. Admin (Extends User)
Purpose: Provides administrative control over doctors, patients, appointments, billing, system reports, and feedback.

Attributes (Fields):
(Inherits all attributes from User)
Methods:
addDoctor(): void — Registers a new doctor into the system with validation
removeDoctor(): void — Removes a doctor and cleans up associated records
addPatient(): void — Registers a new patient into the hospital
removePatient(): void — Deletes patient profile and linked records
manageUsers(): void — Manages account activation and profile edits
manageAppointments(): void — Views, updates status, or reschedules appointments
manageBilling(): void — Generates and processes patient bills
viewSystemReports(): void — Displays analytics on total patients, appointments, and revenues
viewFeedback(): void — Reviews submitted patient feedback and ratings
2. Patient Queue & Notification Modules
🚦 5. QueueManager
Purpose: Controls live OPD patient queueing, priority assignment, queue removal, and per-doctor waiting time calculations.

Attributes (Fields):
(Interacts with queue database table and live scanner input)
Methods:
addPatient(): void — Adds patient into active waiting queue with priority (Emergency, Senior, Normal, etc.)
removePatient(): void — Removes patient from queue upon treatment completion
displayQueue(): void — Views entire system live waiting queue
displayQueue(int doctorId): void — Displays doctor-specific queue sorted by priority & arrival
calculateWaitingTime(): void — Validates Queue ID and estimates waiting time per doctor ($N \times 15\text{ mins}$)
prioritizeEmergency(): void — Elevates patient queue status to Emergency
⏰ 6. Reminder
Purpose: Manages active reminders for patient appointments, medicine schedules, and vaccination alerts.

Attributes (Fields):
(Interacts with reminders table)
Methods:
sendReminder(): void — Displays pending active reminders for a patient
markCompleted(): void — Validates Reminder ID and marks reminder status as completed (Sent)
3. Clinical & Auxiliary Services Modules
📋 7. MedicalRecord
Purpose: Represents patient medical history entries and diagnosis records.

Attributes (Fields):
public int historyId — Medical history record ID
public int patientId — Associated patient ID
public String disease — Diagnosed condition/disease name
public String description — Detailed clinical description/notes
Methods:
MedicalRecord() — Default constructor
MedicalRecord(int, int, String, String) — Parameterized constructor
addRecord(): void — Appends a new medical history record
updateRecord(): void — Updates existing record description
viewRecord(): void — Displays history records
fetchMedicalHistoryList(int): LinkedList<MedicalRecord> — Fetches medical history list into data structure
🥗 8. DietPlan
Purpose: Generates smart nutritional meal plans tailored to specific patient medical conditions.

Attributes (Fields):
String disease — Target medical condition (e.g., Diabetes, Hypertension)
String breakfast — Recommended breakfast items
String lunch — Recommended lunch meal
String snacks — Evening snack options
String dinner — Recommended dinner meal
String water — Recommended daily fluid intake
String avoidFoods — Foods to avoid
Methods:
generateDiet(): void — Creates and saves customized diet plan
viewDietPlan(): void — Displays active patient diet plan
🧪 9. LabTest
Purpose: Manages diagnostic laboratory test bookings, results, and report generation.

Attributes (Fields):
int labTestId — Unique lab test record ID
Methods:
bookLabTest(): void — Schedules a new lab test
updateResult(): void — Uploads test results and diagnosis
viewReport(): void — Displays completed lab test report
manageLabTests(): void — Admin/Doctor lab test control panel
💊 10. Pharmacy
Purpose: Displays hospital pharmacy info and manages medicine inventory stock.

Attributes (Fields):
String pharmacyName — Pharmacy name
String address — Hospital pharmacy location/address
Methods:
displayPharmacy(): void — Displays pharmacy location, medicine stock, expiry dates, and unit prices
🔍 11. DoctorFinder
Purpose: Assists patients in finding available doctors filtered by specialty.

Attributes (Fields):
(Utility query class)
Methods:
searchBySpecialization(): void — Searches and lists doctors by domain (Cardiology, Pediatrics, etc.)
4. Finance & Communication Modules
💳 12. Billing
Purpose: Handles hospital invoice generation, fee payments, and downloadable receipt generation.

Attributes (Fields):
int billId — Billing invoice ID
int patientId — Associated patient ID
double amount — Total bill amount
String paymentMode — Mode (Cash, UPI, Card)
String status — Payment status (Pending/Paid)
Methods:
makePayment(): void — Processes patient fee payment
viewBill(): void — Displays itemized bill details
downloadBill(): void — Exports payment receipt text file
⭐ 13. Feedback
Purpose: Collects patient ratings, reviews, and feedback for attending doctors.

Attributes (Fields):
(Interacts with feedback table)
Methods:
submitFeedback(): void — Submits rating (1–5 stars) and comments for a doctor
💬 14. Discussion
Purpose: Facilitates direct messaging and follow-up communication between patients and doctors.

Attributes (Fields):
(Interacts with discussion table)
Methods:
sendMessage(): void — Sends a message query to doctor
viewConversation(): void — Displays complete message thread between patient and doctor
5. Infrastructure & System Utilities
📊 15. Dashboard
Purpose: Renders quick statistical summary widgets for patients and doctors upon login.

Attributes (Fields):
(Queries live database stats)
Methods:
showPatientDashboard(): void — Displays appointments, pending reminders, and unpaid bills for patient
showDoctorDashboard(): void — Displays today’s appointments, waiting queue size, and average doctor rating
🏥 16. Hospital
Purpose: Holds static hospital metadata and displays active departments.

Attributes (Fields):
String hospitalName — Hospital name
String address — Hospital location address
Methods:
displayHospital(): void — Displays hospital contact details, emergency helpline numbers, and floor department directory
📜 17. AuditLog
Purpose: Tracks system activities using data structures (Stack) for administrative compliance.

Attributes (Fields):
Stack<LogEntry> logStack — In-memory stack of recent operational activities
(Inner Class LogEntry: logId, userId, operation, tableName, timestamp)
Methods:
viewLogs(): void — Displays recent database operations (INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE) for security audits
🔌 18. DBConnection
Purpose: Singleton database connector establishing JDBC connection to MySQL database.

Attributes (Fields):
private static final String url — MySQL JDBC URL (jdbc:mysql://localhost:3307/HealthConnect)
private static final String username — Database user (root)
private static final String password — Database password
public static Connection conn — Active SQL Connection instance
Methods:
public static void initialize(): void — Initializes or re-opens database connection if closed
🚀 19. Main
Purpose: Application entry point hosting interactive console menus and navigation routing for Patients, Doctors, and Admins.

Attributes (Fields):
public static User loggedInUser — Currently authenticated user session instance
Methods:
public static void main(String[] args): void — System entry point driving main execution loop
public static void logActivity(int userId, String operation, String tableName): void — Logs administrative/user activity into database and audit log
